> 
> I'm also worried though about the AI system training to the test, rather than producing the truly best response. I'm not sure though that there's any way to handle that. But it strikes me as an issue because XAI might give the least cost for the highest rate of AI hallucination. So maybe we need to also consider metrics about how good these models are, and how applicable the tools are to various tasks, that do not just come from the feedback.
> 
> I would also like to keep the core of the abstraction quite general. So, I might want to reuse the core in a non-chat environment, and where thumbs-up-down are not the only form of feedback. But I will mostly be engaging with it through chat, so I want that streamlined.
