> ```python
> @dataclass
> class ChatTask:
>     task_id: str
>     conversation_id: str
>     turn_id: str
> 
>     user_message: str
>     conversation_context: dict[str, Any] = field(default_factory=dict)
> 
>     # Product constraints, possibly supplied by user/UI/defaults.
>     max_cost_usd: float | None = None
>     max_latency_s: float | None = None
>     requires_fresh_information: bool = False
>     requires_high_assurance: bool = False
> 
>     created_at: datetime | None = None
> ```
> 
> ```python
> @dataclass
> class ChatResponse:
>     message: str
>     artifact_ids: list[str] = field(default_factory=list)
>     operation_ids: list[str] = field(default_factory=list)
> 
>     # Makes an initial response's status legible to the user/UI.
>     status: Literal["final", "provisional"] = "final"
> ```
> 
> ```python
> @dataclass
> class FeedbackEvent:
>     task_id: str
>     source: Literal["user", "evaluator", "test", "system"]
>     kind: str                         # "thumb", "rating", "correction", "citation_check", ...
>     value: Any                        # True/False, numeric score, structured result
>     metadata: dict[str, Any] = field(default_factory=dict)
>     created_at: datetime | None = None
> ```
> 
> A thumbs-up is simply:
> 
> ```python
> FeedbackEvent(
>     task_id="task_123",
>     source="user",
>     kind="thumb",
>     value=True,
> )
> ```
> 
> ---
> 
> # 2. Plans: what the policy selects
> 
> The policy selects a plan—not just a model. A plan can specify models, tool configurations, verification, budgets, and follow-up behavior.
> 
> ```python
> @dataclass
> class ToolCall:
>     tool_name: str
>     arguments: dict[str, Any]
>     call_config: dict[str, Any] = field(default_factory=dict)
> ```
> 
> ```python
> @dataclass
> class VerificationPolicy:
>     mode: Literal[
>         "none",
>         "self_check",
>         "claim_check",
>         "independent_review",
>     ] = "none"
> 
>     # May be a model ID or a configured evaluator name.
>     reviewer: str | None = None
> ```
> 
> ```python
> @dataclass
> class DeliveryPolicy:
>     mode: Literal[
>         "never",               # Store result, but do not message user.
>         "on_material_result",  # Notify only if it changes/adds meaningful value.
>         "on_completion",       # Notify whenever this work finishes.
>         "on_user_request",     # Store silently until user asks.
>         "digest",              # Bundle updates later.
>     ] = "never"
> 
>     max_updates: int = 1
>     materiality_threshold: float = 0.5
> ```
> 
> ```python
> @dataclass
> class ExecutionPlan:
>     plan_id: str
>     task_id: str
> 
>     primary_model: str
>     initial_tools: list[ToolCall] = field(default_factory=list)
> 
>     verification: VerificationPolicy = field(default_factory=VerificationPolicy)
>     delivery: DeliveryPolicy = field(default_factory=DeliveryPolicy)
> 
>     max_cost_usd: float | None = None
>     max_latency_s: float | None = None
> 
>     # Whether the planner should wait for required operations before replying.
>     response_strategy: Literal[
>         "wait",
>         "provisional_then_continue",
>         "defer",
>     ] = "wait"
> 
>     rationale: str | None = None       # Logged for observability/debugging.
> ```
> 
> Examples:
> 
> ```python
> # Cheap direct answer.
> ExecutionPlan(
>     plan_id="...",
>     task_id="...",
>     primary_model="openai:gpt-5-mini",
> )
> ```
> 
> ```python
> # Personalized answer using configured memory retrieval.
> ExecutionPlan(
>     plan_id="...",
>     task_id="...",
>     primary_model="gemini:flash",
>     initial_tools=[
>         ToolCall(
>             tool_name="memory.retrieve",
>             arguments={"query": "How should I prioritize my current projects?"},
>             call_config={
>                 "collections": ["projects", "preferences"],
>                 "top_k": 8,
>                 "min_score": 0.60,
>                 "reranker": "cross_encoder_v2",
>             },
>         ),
>     ],
> )
> ```
> 
> ```python
> # Fresh/high-assurance factual answer.
> ExecutionPlan(
>     plan_id="...",
>     task_id="...",
>     primary_model="openai:gpt-5",
>     initial_tools=[
>         ToolCall(
>             tool_name="openai.web_search",
>             arguments={"query": "..."},
>             call_config={"max_results": 8, "trusted_sources_only": True},
>         ),
>     ],
>     verification=VerificationPolicy(
>         mode="claim_check",
>         reviewer="openai:gpt-5-mini",
>     ),
> )
> ```
> 
> ---
> 
> # 3. Durable asynchronous work: operations and artifacts
> 
> An `Operation` is a unit of executable work. It may be a tool invocation, model call, evaluator, or workflow. Its output is represented by one or more durable `Artifact`s.
> 
> ```python
> @dataclass
> class BudgetReservation:
>     max_cost_usd: float | None = None
>     max_tokens: int | None = None
>     max_latency_s: float | None = None
> ```
> 
> ```python
> @dataclass
> class Operation:
>     operation_id: str
>     task_id: str
>     conversation_id: str | None
> 
>     kind: Literal[
>         "tool",
>         "model",
>         "evaluation",
>         "workflow",
>         "human_review",
>     ]
>     spec: dict[str, Any]
> 
>     state: Literal[
>         "queued",
>         "running",
>         "succeeded",
>         "failed",
>         "cancelled",
>         "expired",
>     ] = "queued"
> 
>     # IDs of operations or artifacts which must resolve first.
>     depends_on: list[str] = field(default_factory=list)
> 
>     idempotency_key: str | None = None
>     priority: int = 0
>     deadline_at: datetime | None = None
>     budget: BudgetReservation | None = None
> 
>     visibility: Literal[
>         "internal",            # No context or user-visible effect by default.
>         "context_only",        # Result becomes available to future model calls.
>         "notify_user",        # May produce an async user update.
>         "approval_required",  # Cannot take follow-on action without approval.
>     ] = "context_only"
> 
>     created_at: datetime | None = None
>     started_at: datetime | None = None
>     completed_at: datetime | None = None
>     error: str | None = None
> ```
> 
> ```python
> @dataclass
> class Provenance:
>     source: str                        # model ID, tool name, URI, user, etc.
>     created_at: datetime
>     parent_artifact_ids: list[str] = field(default_factory=list)
>     metadata: dict[str, Any] = field(default_factory=dict)
> ```
> 
> ```python
> @dataclass
> class QualityMetadata:
>     confidence: float | None = None
>     evaluator_scores: dict[str, float] = field(default_factory=dict)
>     is_stale: bool = False
> ```
> 
> ```python
> @dataclass
> class Artifact:
>     artifact_id: str
>     operation_id: str
> 
>     kind: str                          # "search_results", "memory_hits", "model_response", ...
>     content_ref: str                   # Object-store or database reference.
>     summary: str | None = None
> 
>     provenance: Provenance | None = None
>     quality: QualityMetadata | None = None
>     expires_at: datetime | None = None
> ```
> 
> An operation can expose a future reference before it finishes:
> 
> ```python
> @dataclass(frozen=True)
> class OperationFuture:
>     operation_id: str
> ```
> 
> ---
> 
> # 4. Execution API
> 
> This is the API used by the policy/planner to create an asynchronous workflow.
> 
> ```python
> class OpsAPI(Protocol):
>     def submit(
>         self,
>         *,
>         task_id: str,
>         conversation_id: str | None,
>         kind: Literal["tool", "model", "evaluation", "workflow", "human_review"],
>         spec: dict[str, Any],
>         depends_on: list[str | OperationFuture] | None = None,
>         visibility: Literal[
>             "internal",
>             "context_only",
>             "notify_user",
>             "approval_required",
>         ] = "context_only",
>         priority: int = 0,
>         deadline_at: datetime | None = None,
>         budget: BudgetReservation | None = None,
>         idempotency_key: str | None = None,
>     ) -> OperationFuture:
>         """Queue work and return a durable reference immediately."""
>         ...
> 
>     def await_artifacts(
>         self,
>         futures: list[OperationFuture],
>         *,
>         timeout_s: float | None = None,
>     ) -> dict[str, Artifact]:
>         """Wait for successful primary artifacts of the given operations."""
>         ...
> 
>     def get_operation(self, operation_id: str) -> Operation:
>         ...
> 
>     def get_artifact(self, artifact_id: str) -> Artifact:
>         ...
> 
>     def cancel(self, operation_id: str) -> None:
>         ...
> ```
> 
> Example: concurrent retrieval and web research, followed by synthesis.
> 
> ```python
> memory = ops.submit(
>     task_id=task.task_id,
>     conversation_id=task.conversation_id,
>     kind="tool",
>     spec={
>         "tool_name": "memory.retrieve",
>         "arguments": {"query": task.user_message},
>         "call_config": {"top_k": 6, "collections": ["projects", "preferences"]},
>     },
> )
> 
> web = ops.submit(
>     task_id=task.task_id,
>     conversation_id=task.conversation_id,
>     kind="tool",
>     spec={
>         "tool_name": "openai.web_search",
>         "arguments": {"query": task.user_message},
>         "call_config": {"max_results": 6},
>     },
> )
> 
> answer = ops.submit(
>     task_id=task.task_id,
>     conversation_id=task.conversation_id,
>     kind="model",
>     depends_on=[memory, web],
>     spec={
>         "model_id": "openai:gpt-5",
>         "inputs": {
>             "task": task.user_message,
>             "memory_operation": memory.operation_id,
>             "web_operation": web.operation_id,
>         },
>     },
> )
> ```
> 
> The synthesis operation does not begin until its dependencies succeed, but the retrieval and search operations can execute in parallel.
> 
> ---
> 
> # 5. Durable conversation and workspace state
> 
> Do not mutate the canonical chat transcript when async work finishes. Store completed work in explicit, versioned state; the context builder can include relevant state in the next model invocation.
> 
> ```python
> @dataclass
> class StatePatch:
>     scope: Literal[
>         "turn",
>         "conversation",
>         "project",
>         "user_memory",
>     ]
>     target_id: str
> 
>     # RFC 6902 JSON Patch operations.
>     patch: list[dict[str, Any]]
> 
>     provenance: Provenance
>     confidence: float = 1.0
